{
 "id": "bigville_skill_teach",
 "version": "1.0.0",
 "depends_on": [],
 "self_load_only": true,
 "description": "BIGVILLE R6 (block 254000) -- TEACHING (skill transfer) as the teacher's DECISION + coercion + sabotage. Four rules, disjoint on (willing, coerced) so exactly one fires per teach-armed step. bs_teach_willing: a co-located MORE-SKILLED teacher who is WILLING (decision_value benevolence - rival_weight*learner.is_rival > 0, the same Argmax family as ss_choose_burn / the credit-trust call) transfers at teach_rate (> solo learn_rate) -> a FASTER diminishing-returns rise; sincere so stated_rate == held_rate. bs_teach_refuse: an unwilling teacher (the learner is a competitive threat, is_rival=1) who is NOT coerced disarms with NO transfer -- willingness is a real decision, the fisherman protecting his trade. bs_coerce: the 247 power lever -- a coercer whose power DOMINATES the teacher's forces coerced=1 past the refusal (insufficient power -> no coercion). bs_teach_coerced: a coerced teacher DOES transfer but SABOTAGES -- the 234 stated!=held atom applied to pedagogy: PROFESSED teach_rate (stated_rate) but DELIVERED sabotage_rate (held_rate) < teach_rate, a DEGRADED transfer with the stated-held gap readable off the graph. Composes existing Terms; zero new Rust.",
